// 3506
[dbrow_3506]
table=dbtable_40
data=col0,37
data=col1,30
data=col3,black_placeholder,I was there, in the year of Croesus. The year the fungus killed fifty thousand people, and the Tenth Legion were annihilated.,sound_51393,585,false,false,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_01,It was the Second Age, not long after the end of the Kharidian Campaign.,sound_51396,302,true,false,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_01,An expedition returned from the Unquiet Ocean with a very unusual species of fungus.,sound_51392,352,false,false,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_01,The fools thought they could turn it into a weapon. A botanical plague they could unleash on the enemies of the Empire.,sound_51400,460,false,true,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_02,They called it Croesus. Its spores infested the bodies of the dead, spreading and growing.,sound_51401,435,true,false,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_02,They fed it slaves, tested it, burned away weakness, forced it to evolve. They did their jobs far too well.,sound_51402,520,false,false,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_02,After one serious breach, they were ordered to cease their work. They didn't.,sound_51390,380,false,true,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_03,Inevitably, Croesus broke free into the city again, choking the streets with its putrescent growth.,sound_51395,485,true,false,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_03,Nothing could stop it. Priests and guards alike were powerless, and their bodies only served to fuel its flourishing.,sound_51398,500,false,true,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_04,I was with the Tenth Legion when we were recalled from the border to combat the infestation.,sound_51388,380,true,false,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_04,After days of fighting, my wings ached and my dragonfire was spent.,sound_51389,375,false,false,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_04,We razed miles of city to contain it. The Legion were almost completely wiped out. It still wasn't enough.,sound_51404,505,false,true,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_05,In the end Lord Zaros was forced to intervene personally. He *quarantined* this whole district - simply buried it beneath the earth.,sound_51394,600,true,false,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_05,I thought the remains of Croesus were destroyed. They assured me they were destroyed!,sound_51387,395,false,true,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_06,They say that of all the Elder Gods, Bik holds intelligent life in the greatest contempt.,sound_51403,380,true,false,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_06,She must have found Croesus beneath the graveyard and revived it. Even now it feeds on the ancient dead.,sound_51399,453,false,false,true,true
data=col3,egwd_croesus_front_cutscene_06,It's already massacred every defender on this front. If we don't drive it back, it will tear the cathedral to pieces.,sound_51397,525,false,true,true,true

