// 4410
[dbrow_4410]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,56
data=col1,1
data=col2,dbrow_4408
data=col3,Senntisten Dig Site
data=col6,Senntisten was the capital city of the Zarosian Empire during the Second and Third Age...
data=col7,Your research team has discovered lots of materials from Senntisten.
data=col8,6000
data=col10,2
data=col10,4
data=col10,8
data=col10,12
data=col10,24
data=col11,105
data=col17,1
data=col17,2

// 4411
[dbrow_4411]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,182
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_apex_cap
data=col3,The apex cap was worn by the Zarosian priesthood in Senntisten. The strange shape of the cap represents the tendrils that Zaros used to defeat the hydra deity Loarnab.
data=col4,60
data=col5,obj_51880
data=col6,obj_51881

// 4412
[dbrow_4412]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,183
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_curse_tablet
data=col3,Magicians in the empire would create curse tablets. Sheets of metal on which the name of an enemy would be inscribed. The tablet was then buried in a graveyard so that dark spirits would know the name of the target.
data=col4,60
data=col5,obj_51882
data=col6,obj_51883

// 4413
[dbrow_4413]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,184
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_decorative_amphora
data=col3,Citizens would use intricate and beautifully decorated amphoras to display their wealth and status. Many would display religious lessons or parables as a further sign of the citizen's devotion.
data=col4,63
data=col5,obj_51884
data=col6,obj_51885

// 4414
[dbrow_4414]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,185
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_funerary_urn_of_miasma
data=col3,These urns were used by the ancient priests of Senntisten in funeral rites. Miasma would be used to symbolically guide the spirit to Erebus as the miasma would create a trail the spirit could follow.
data=col4,67
data=col5,obj_51886
data=col6,obj_51887

// 4415
[dbrow_4415]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,186
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_funerary_urn_of_blood
data=col3,The blood of the dead was collected in these funerary urns as a reminder of the life lost. The urns would then be magically infused so that the blood could remain as a constant source of ancient magick creating a lasting legacy for the deceased.
data=col4,66
data=col5,obj_51888
data=col6,obj_51889

// 4416
[dbrow_4416]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,187
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_funerary_urn_of_ice
data=col3,The urn of ice would be used in ancient Senntisten funerals to chill and thus preserve the body of the deceased. The body would be frozen by the magic and the urn would keep it cold and holding back the ravages of decay.
data=col4,63
data=col5,obj_51890
data=col6,obj_51891

// 4417
[dbrow_4417]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,188
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_funerary_urn_of_shadow
data=col3,Shadow urns were used in Senntisten funerals to obscure the deceased's soul from dark spirits on the journey to Erebus.
data=col4,60
data=col5,obj_51892
data=col6,obj_51893

// 4418
[dbrow_4418]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,189
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_funerary_urn_of_smoke
data=col3,Urns empowered with the ancient magick of smoke would be used as a marker for the deceased. Placed at their grave for days after their passing, anyone would be able to look in the air and see a trail of smoke indicating a life lost.
data=col4,62
data=col5,obj_51894
data=col6,obj_51895

// 4419
[dbrow_4419]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,190
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_gladiator_helmet
data=col3,The colosseum was a great spectacle in the empire and one of the most popular forms of entertainment. Gladiators could find themselves elevated from criminals to beloved heroes. Few survived to enjoy the adulation for long.
data=col4,66
data=col5,obj_51896
data=col6,obj_51897

// 4420
[dbrow_4420]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,191
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_gladiator_sword
data=col3,Gladiators would be armed with two weapons, a sword and a net. Over time a gladiator would favour a particular sword and many would give their swords names to terrify their opponents and impress the crowds.
data=col4,66
data=col5,obj_51898
data=col6,obj_51899

// 4421
[dbrow_4421]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,192
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_hand_of_the_ancients
data=col3,A strange sculpture representing the ancient elements. The hand of ancients was placed in the homes of citizens to ward off bad spirits that might try and sneak inside to cause mischief.
data=col4,62
data=col5,obj_51900
data=col6,obj_51901

// 4422
[dbrow_4422]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,193
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_infula_robes
data=col3,These robes were worn by the members of the church as a sign of their religious purity. They would be immaculately maintained and washed in a mixture of perfumes giving them a distinct aroma.
data=col4,62
data=col5,obj_51902
data=col6,obj_51903

// 4423
[dbrow_4423]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,194
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_inquisitor_seal
data=col3,Due to their secretive nature it was necessary for the members of the Inquisition to have an official badge of office in cases of mistaken identity. These badges were subtly enchanted so that they would be impossible to forge.
data=col4,64
data=col5,obj_51904
data=col6,obj_51905

// 4424
[dbrow_4424]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,195
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_inquisitor_ceremonial_armour
data=col3,This armour would be used for secret ceremonies among the Inquisition or when members would need to gather, such as in the Inquisition office. They incorporated slightly strange proportions to try and disguise the species of the wearer so that as much anonymity as possible could be maintained.
data=col4,64
data=col5,obj_51906
data=col6,obj_51907

// 4425
[dbrow_4425]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,196
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_inquisitor_ceremonial_mask
data=col3,The sinister mask of the Inquisitor was designed purely to hide their features. The mouth was sealed shut to imply the silent power of the Inquisition as well as their oath to secrecy.
data=col4,64
data=col5,obj_51908
data=col6,obj_51909

// 4426
[dbrow_4426]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,197
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_loarnab_rod
data=col3,This rod was worn by physicians around the empire as a symbol of their craft. Not only did it demonstrate their healing skills, by referencing Loarnab's unnatural powers of regeneration, but also served as a reminder that anything can be overcome.
data=col4,63
data=col5,obj_51910
data=col6,obj_51911

// 4427
[dbrow_4427]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,198
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_model_chariot
data=col3,The demon drawn chariot races of Senntisten were a marvel to behold. Mighty demons would drag a human or vampyre chariot rider across the skies of the city in magnificent races against other teams. It was one of the most popular forms of entertainment in the city.
data=col4,67
data=col5,obj_51912
data=col6,obj_51913

// 4428
[dbrow_4428]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,199
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_carving_loarnab
data=col3,This image depicts the fall of Loarnab, one of the most popular religious stories in the empire. It clearly shows Zaros's triumph over the hydra god.
data=col4,67
data=col5,obj_51914
data=col6,obj_51915

