// 7592
[dbrow_7592]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,201
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_necromantic_focus
data=col3,This book - the Glacienomicom, aka the Book of Ice - details Orcus's discovery of the existence of Rasial and his exploits in the west. It also has a treatise on using animated skeletons as a defensive wall of bone.
data=col4,86
data=col5,obj_55249
data=col6,obj_55250

// 7593
[dbrow_7593]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,202
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_necromantic_focus
data=col3,This book - the Fumonomicom, aka the Book of Smoke - details how Orcus learned that Rasial used to be a guardian of magic and runes. It also has a treatise on shrouding oneself with ghosts, making it harder for enemies to target you.
data=col4,86
data=col5,obj_55251
data=col6,obj_55252

// 7594
[dbrow_7594]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,203
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_necromantic_focus
data=col3,This book - the Umbranomicom, aka the Book of Shadow - details Orcus's revelation that Rasial was a once-human follower of Guthix. It also has a treatise on using a phantom - the Spirit of Death - to make enemies easier to kill.
data=col4,86
data=col5,obj_55253
data=col6,obj_55254

// 7595
[dbrow_7595]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,204
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_necromantic_focus
data=col3,This book - the Sanguinomicom, aka the Book of Blood - details how Orcus tasked the Heriditas Expedition to track down the location of the tomb of Rasial. It also has a treatise on transferring one's own life essence to prolong zombie minions.
data=col4,86
data=col5,obj_55255
data=col6,obj_55256

// 7596
[dbrow_7596]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,62
data=col1,2
data=col2,dbrow_2802
data=col3,Nom-Nom-Nom-Nom
data=col4,86
data=col6,Orcus's collected writings on necromancy, and Gielinor's first necromancer.
data=col7,The five books work like a quintych! While coherent in their own right, certain sections of the books lead into parts of the other books in sequence. The team found a hidden message but can't decipher it further: 0216N0724E
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49885,1

