// 7785
[dbrow_7785]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,The <col=FFCB05>ritual selection interface</col> allows you to choose a ritual to perform.
data=col5,interface_1224:com_3
data=col6,-1

// 7786
[dbrow_7786]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,Each ritual has different requirements. Here you can <col=FFCB05>view the requirements</col> needed to select the ritual, as well as the ritual components you'll need to <col=FFCB05>set up on your ritual site</col>.
data=col5,interface_1224:com_12
data=col6,-1
data=col21,interface_1224:com_12,-1

// 7787
[dbrow_7787]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,Rituals also require a <col=FFCB05>focus object</col>, which is consumed upon completing the ritual. Some rituals may have a choice of <col=FFCB05>multiple focus objects</col>.
data=col5,interface_1224:com_20
data=col6,-1
data=col21,interface_1224:com_20,-1

// 7788
[dbrow_7788]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,Once a ritual has been completed, you are <col=FFCB05>rewarded with the ritual's output</col>.
data=col5,interface_1224:com_26
data=col6,-1
data=col21,interface_1224:com_26,-1

// 7789
[dbrow_7789]
table=dbtable_71
data=col0,Necromancy
data=col2,dbrow_7790
data=col3,dbrow_7790
data=col4,dbrow_7790

// 7790
[dbrow_7790]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,The <col=FFCB05>ritual information window</col> displays everything you need to set up for your selected ritual.
data=col5,interface_1223:com_29
data=col6,-1

// 7791
[dbrow_7791]
table=dbtable_71
data=col0,Necromancy
data=col2,dbrow_7792
data=col3,dbrow_7792
data=col4,dbrow_7792

// 7792
[dbrow_7792]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,Different <col=FFCB05>communion ritual</col> focus objects give <col=FFCB05>different amounts of souls</col>. Higher-levelled communion rituals, and stronger focus objects will give <col=FFCB05>more souls</col>.
data=col5,interface_1224:com_26
data=col6,-1
data=col16,ritual_icon_necromancy_soul_attraction_active_1

// 7793
[dbrow_7793]
table=dbtable_71
data=col0,Necromancy
data=col2,dbrow_7794
data=col3,dbrow_7794
data=col4,dbrow_7794

// 7794
[dbrow_7794]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,Different <col=FFCB05>ensoul ritual</col> focus objects give <col=FFCB05>different ensouled materials</col> - including <col=FFCB05>ensouled bars</col>, <col=FFCB05>thread</col>, and <col=FFCB05>cloth</col>.
data=col5,interface_1224:com_26
data=col6,-1
data=col20,obj_55614

// 7795
[dbrow_7795]
table=dbtable_71
data=col0,Necromancy
data=col2,dbrow_7796
data=col3,dbrow_7796
data=col4,dbrow_7796

// 7796
[dbrow_7796]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,<col=FFCB05>A ritual disturbance has appeared!</col><br>Ritual disturbances will occasionally appear while performing rituals. <col=FFCB05>Interact with them to gain a reward</col>.

// 7797
[dbrow_7797]
table=dbtable_71
data=col0,Necromancy
data=col2,dbrow_7798
data=col2,dbrow_7799
data=col3,dbrow_7798
data=col3,dbrow_7799
data=col4,dbrow_7798
data=col4,dbrow_7799
data=col11,true

// 7798
[dbrow_7798]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,Ritual disturbances will <col=FFCB05>appear more often</col> the higher your <col=FFCB05>soul attraction</col> is.
data=col5,interface_1225:com_1
data=col6,-1
data=col16,ritual_icon_necromancy_soul_attraction_active_1

// 7799
[dbrow_7799]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,<col=FFCB05>Soul attraction</col> can be <col=FFCB05>increased</col>, and <col=FFCB05>decreased</col>, through the use of <col=FFCB05>alteration glyphs</col>. Alteration glyphs are drawn on glyph spots in your ritual site, and are unlocked as you <col=FFCB05>level up Necromancy</col>.
data=col5,interface_1225:com_1
data=col6,-1
data=col16,ritual_icon_necromancy_soul_attraction_active_1

// 7800
[dbrow_7800]
table=dbtable_71
data=col0,Necromancy
data=col2,dbrow_7801
data=col3,dbrow_7801
data=col4,dbrow_7801

// 7801
[dbrow_7801]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,<col=FFCB05>You've completed a ritual!</col><br>Any <col=FFCB05>output</col> you are rewarded with can be found in the <col=FFCB05>ritual chest</col>, by <col=FFCB05>Malignius</col>.
data=col11,3

// 7802
[dbrow_7802]
table=dbtable_71
data=col0,Necromancy
data=col2,dbrow_7803
data=col3,dbrow_7803
data=col4,dbrow_7803

// 7803
[dbrow_7803]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,Next to the <col=FFCB05>ritual chest</col> you can find the <col=FFCB05>focus storage</col>. This allows you to store <col=FFCB05>focus objects</col>, which are <col=FFCB05>automatically used</col> when selecting a ritual, as well as to set up the same ritual upon completion.
data=col11,3

// 7804
[dbrow_7804]
